The export contains **412 unique reports** merged into #4471. It has 427 rows; 15 repeated report IDs count once. The reports point to two different date problems, so #4471 should not stay as one undivided bug.

## Problems found

| Cause | Reports | Evidence | GitHub issue |
| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
| `parser` | **379** | 204 app, 150 email, 25 form; all 11 tenants | [#1 — month-first parser](https://github.com/damian08k/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) |
| `hint` | **33** | 33 booking-v3 form submissions across three day-first tenants | [#2 — booking-v3 hint](https://github.com/damian08k/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) |

## Desk update · 05 October

The course page reports that #4471 is closed. The desk marked the `parser` cause fixed with `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. It marked the `hint` cause won't fix because the booking-v3 form was retired.

| Cause | Desk outcome | Tracking issue |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` | Fixed | [#1 — completed](https://github.com/damian08k/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) |
| `hint` | Won't fix · booking-v3 form retired | [#2 — not planned](https://github.com/damian08k/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) |

## Why they are separate

The shared parser treats dates as month-first. For tenants whose locale writes day first, that can reverse the day and month. This is the `parser` cause.

The `hint` cause is limited to booking-v3 forms in day-first tenants. The form tells people to enter `MM/DD/YYYY`, while the tenant's date handling reads day first. The form hint creates a different failure from the shared parser.

The tenant locale and booking form determine the cause. The intake tag is only a guess and disagrees with that classification on 38 unique reports. The desk noted five reports as one-day moves; all five remain in the `parser` group under the tenant and form rules.

## Counting rule

The report export overlaps: count each report ID once. This leaves 412 reports across the two causes, matching the desk's total after deduplication.

